data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"I have everything I need to write the design. Package version is 0.3.0 (latest). Tokens: `--color-cat-1` (blue), `--color-cat-6` (orange), `--color-cat-10` (lime), etc. The categorical palette is the natural choice for greeting colours.\n\nDesign decisions (small, one pass):\n- **Greeting**: \"Hello from Codesweep!\" — actually let me pick something simple: \"Hello, world!\" is classic but plain. The campaign is hello2952. Greeting: \"Hello from the campaign!\" Let me just choose: **\"Hello, world!\"** with a subtitle maybe. Keep it small. I'll choose greeting text: `Hello, world!`\n- **Colours**: three colour buttons using categorical tokens: blue (`--color-cat-1`), orange (`--color-cat-6`), violet (`--color-cat-5`). Default greeting colour: blue (`--color-cat-1`).\n- **Buttons**: three DS `Button`s labelled \"Blue\", \"Orange\", \"Violet\". Variants: keep simple — `secondary` for all? Or match? Keep simple: variant=\"secondary\", size=\"md\". Actually primary for the active one could add state complexity; keep design small: all `secondary`.\n- **Layout**: `AppShell` wrapping everything; `Header` with title \"Colour Greeting\" (no nav); content area centered: an `h1` greeting in the selected token colour, and a row of the three Buttons beneath it; `Footer` with a short line like \"Built with @codesweep-ai/ui\".\n- Maybe use `Page` for the content inset? The catalog has Page (experimental, since 0.3.0 — package is 0.3.0, so it exists). Keep it small: AppShell + Header + Page + Footer? Page is \"experimental\" but available. Simpler: just AppShell, Header, Footer, and a centered div. The mission requires Header, Footer, Button, tokens — beyond those the design is mine. Keep minimal: no extra components. Maybe a Card to hold the greeting? That adds a component stylesheet. Keep it stupidly simple: no Card.\n\nLayout specifics without pixels: greeting centered horizontally and vertically in the content area, button row centered below the greeting with a small gap.\n\nState: useState holding the current colour token name; clicking a button sets it.\n\nNow write DESIGN.md in ~/hello-app, commit, then push to developer and dispatch.\n\nDESIGN.md content plan:\n\n```md\n# Design — Colour Greeting\n\n## What the interface is\nA single page that shows a greeting and lets the viewer recolour it with a button click.\n\n## Building blocks (from @codesweep-ai/ui)\n- AppShell — outermost wrapper\n- Header — top bar, title \"Colour Greeting\", no nav items, no actions\n- Footer — bottom bar with one line of text: \"Built with the codesweep design system\"\n- Button — the colour buttons (variant=\"secondary\", size=\"md\")\n- Colour tokens — greeting colours come only from --color-* tokens\n\n## Greeting\nText: \"Hello, world!\"\nRendered as a single large heading (h1). Its colour is the currently selected token.\n\n## Colours\nThree choices, each a design-system token:\n| Button label | Token | Resulting greeting colour |\n| Blue | --color-cat-1 | blue |\n| Orange | --color-cat-6 | orange |\n| Violet | --color-cat-5 | violet |\n\nDefault on load: Blue (--color-cat-1).\n\n## Layout\n- Header at top (via AppShell), Footer at bottom.\n- Content area between them: the greeting heading centred horizontally, with the three Buttons in a row directly beneath it, centred, small even gaps. The group sits in the vertical middle of the content area.\n- No other components.\n\n## Behaviour\n- Clicking a button immediately changes the greeting's colour to that button's token. State held with useState. No persistence, no animation.\n```\n\nKeep it concise. Also note: no hex values anywhere; buttons labelled exactly \"Blue\", \"Orange\", \"Violet\".\n\nThen commit, push to developer, write dispatch file for developer.\n\nThe developer dispatch must contain everything the developer needs (it cannot ask). Its brief (roles/developer.md) already covers most: merge refs/campaign/orchestrator, read DESIGN.md, React+Vite+useState, npm install @codesweep-ai/ui, AppShell/Header/Footer/Button, style imports, tokens, catalog reading hints, bind 0.0.0.0:5173, README with build/serve commands, .gitignore, one pass, report branch + commands. So my dispatch should tell it: implement DESIGN.md per your brief; the ref is there; merge it; report branch and commands. Keep it focused but complete.\n\nLet me write DESIGN.md now."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793342820,"id":"chatcmpl-c22e4e83","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

