data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":", \"content\": \"# Design — Colour Greeting\\n\\nA single page that shows a greeting and lets the viewer change the greeting's\\ncolour by clicking a button.\\n\\n## Building blocks (all from `@codesweep-ai/ui`)\\n\\n- `AppShell` — the outermost wrapper of the page.\\n- `Header` — placed inside `AppShell` at the top. Title: **Colour Greeting**.\\n  No nav items, no actions.\\n- `Footer` — placed inside `AppShell` at the bottom. One line of text:\\n  **Built with the codesweep design system**.\\n- `Button` — used for every colour button, `variant=\\\"secondary\\\"`, `size=\\\"md\\\"`.\\n- Colour tokens — every greeting colour is a `--color-*` token from the design\\n  system. No hex values anywhere in the application.\\n\\nNo other components. Nothing else from the catalog.\\n\\n## Greeting\\n\\nThe exact text **Hello, world!**, rendered as a single large heading (`h1`).\\nIts text colour is the currently selected token.\\n\\n## Colours\\n\\nThree choices, each a design-system token:\\n\\n| Button label | Token           |\\n| ------------ | --------------- |\\n| Blue         | `--color-cat-1` |\\n| Orange       | `--color-cat-6` |\\n| Violet       | `--color-cat-5` |\\n\\nOn first load the greeting uses **Blue** (`--color-cat-1`).\\n\\n## Layout\\n\\n- `Header` at the top, `Footer` at the bottom (both via `AppShell`).\\n- The content area between them holds the greeting heading, horizontally\\n  centred, with the three `Button`s in a row directly beneath it — also\\n  centred, with a small even gap between them. The greeting-plus-buttons group\\n  sits in the vertical middle of the content area.\\n\\n## Behaviour\\n\\n- Clicking a button immediately changes the greeting's colour to that button's\\n  token.\\n- State is held with `useState`. No persistence, no animation, no routing.\\n"},"index":0}]},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793342820,"id":"chatcmpl-c22e4e83","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

